cff-version: 1.2.0
title: PST-Parser
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Gianfranco
    family-names: Barba
abstract: >-
  Supervised fine-tuning and evaluation pipeline for the structural segmentation
  of large language model prompts according to the Prompt Syntax Tree framework.
  Given a natural language prompt, the model extracts its text segments and
  assigns each of them to a node of a hierarchical taxonomy.
keywords:
  - prompt engineering
  - large language models
  - fine-tuning
  - structured extraction
  - software engineering
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/gianfrancobarba/PST-Parser
version: 0.1.0
references:
  - type: thesis
    title: >-
      Prompt Syntax Tree: A Formal Representation for the Analysis and Automatic
      Decomposition of LLM Prompts
    authors:
      - given-names: Giovanni
        family-names: Scorziello
    thesis-type: Master's thesis
    institution:
      name: Università degli Studi di Salerno
    year: 2025
